  "description": "N-1 positive (immortality §6.4: the core speaks N and N-1): a core at proto_version 0.3 or later against a frozen v0.2 worker runs create, attach, prefix and a restart-reattach unchanged. The core offers proto_version \"0.2\" toward the v0.2 worker, and sends exactly v0.2's messages: the connect's timers carry no keepalive_probe_interval, because the frozen v0.2 worker refuses a timers whose key set is not exactly the eight it knows (#114), and the field sent toward it would kill every session there (D29). Toward a 0.3 or 0.4 worker the same core sends the probe field and hello at that worker's version. This sequence is that first half: hello \"0.2\", an ack speaking \"0.2\", and a connect whose timers omit the probe key. The live run against the frozen wheel is the rig (owed).",
  "corpus": [
    "immortality §6.4",
    "5.51",
    "decision 5.29 (D29)",
    "plan.md §3 C3"
  ],
